# Exceptions for the prose half of tools/check_pmids.py.
# Format: <pmid or path>  <written reason>.  A reason is mandatory.
#
# Two kinds, and they are not equivalent:
#
#   <pmid>  skipped entirely. For an identifier the prose quotes ON PURPOSE as
#           being wrong — the correction tables that record what an id used to
#           be. Checking those would flag the documentation of a fix as a bug.
#
#   <path>  existence-only. For a file of bare reference lists: ids with no
#           author or title beside them to diff against. Every id in it is still
#           resolved, so a dead identifier is still caught; only the "does it
#           name this paper" half is dropped, because there is no name.
#
# Adding a line here is a claim that the id cannot be checked, not that it is
# fine. Prefer writing the author's surname next to the id instead.

# --- Files of bare reaction-reference lists (existence-only) ---
docs/figures/urea-cycle.md  VMH reaction provenance: ids listed per reaction id (ARGSL, UREAt, ...) with no author or title anywhere on the line.

# --- Identifiers quoted deliberately as wrong ---
8962261@docs/metabolic-constants.md   metabolic-constants.md correction table: recorded as the WRONG id previously shipped for Miller & Wolin 1996.
